# lsp — language server
File: website/pulled/lsp.oot

Source: openOODA/lsp/docs/

## What it is

The Language Server Protocol server for `.oo` files.
Release tag v0.6.12. Editors speak JSON-RPC over stdio.
Cap grant files come from `${oodar_root}/sec/cap/cap_table.json`
via `--oodar-root`. No hard-coded cap table.
Point the editor at the `lsp` binary. See
`lsp/docs/LSP_SETUP.oot`.

## Surface

Advertised methods (from `lsp/docs/CAPABILITIES.oot`):

| Tier | Methods |
|------|---------|
| Lifecycle | initialize, initialized, shutdown, exit |
| Sync | textDocument/didOpen, didChange, didClose |
| Document | completion, hover, definition, formatting, documentSymbol, codeAction, diagnostic, documentLink, inlayHint |
| Workspace | workspace/executeCommand |

Commands: `ooda.lsp.version`, `ooda.lsp.indexSize`,
`ooda.lsp.echo`, `ooda.lsp.tokenCount`.

Full document sync only (`change: 1`). Incremental sync is
not implemented. Not advertised: rename, references,
signatureHelp, semantic tokens, workspace/symbol.
